      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "A practical example",
          "text": "For ten thank-you gifts at one workplace, prepare a table with recipient, card text and department. Specify whether you need one combined reception drop-off or ten separate handovers: they require different work and may change the quotation."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Delivery at a managed venue",
          "text": "Public-facing venues do not necessarily provide a gift reception service. For offices, hotels, event spaces, universities and clinics, contact the responsible person and verify whether flowers are accepted, where handover may take place and during which window. A building name may be insufficient when a complex has multiple entrances. Do not ask staff to disclose private information about the recipient. If internal access is prohibited, arrange delivery at an authorised point or an agreed alternative address. The venue's rules take priority over a preferred handover plan."
        },
        {
          "heading": "City access and delivery routes",
          "text": "In Milan, checking the route is part of preparing an order. Area B covers much of the city and restricts more polluting vehicles; Area C regulates central access, generally with a charge for eligible vehicles unless exempt. These are distinct rules and also matter for goods transport. Pedestrian streets, driveways and reserved lanes may prevent stopping at the address. Agree on a lawful handover point rather than asking a courier to ignore restrictions. Check current municipal rules for the intended day and vehicle."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Hydration during transport",
          "text": "Cut flowers are affected by dehydration and temperature fluctuations during transport. A water-filled aquabox may help when the arrangement and route allow it: ask whether one is available and suitable for your selected format. The container should remain stable, away from heat sources, with flower heads protected from crushing. Once the gift arrives, remove wrapping that blocks ventilation, prepare a clean vase and follow the stem-specific care instructions. Do not mistake decorative wrapping for a permanent hydration system or leave the bouquet unattended in a hot vehicle."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Flower origin and freshness",
          "text": "Freshness cannot be judged solely by whether a flower comes from a major market. Milan's flower market, the trading channels of Aalsmeer and flower production on the Sanremo Riviera are different parts of the supply chain. Ask about the batch actually available and the characteristics of the variety. Checking petals, leaves and stems is more useful than assuming a harvest date from appearance alone. For an uncommon variety or a specific country of origin, request confirmation before finalising the arrangement and allow for an alternative if unavailable."
        },
        {
          "heading": "A photo before dispatch",
          "text": "A real photograph can help check appearance before delivery, particularly if you are not in Milan. Ask on WhatsApp at +39 379 371 8598 whether you can receive a picture of the finished bouquet before dispatch. Say whether you want to check the overall colour, card or a specific detail. A photograph alone does not prove origin, vase life or storage temperature; its primary value is visual confirmation. To avoid delaying an urgent delivery, agree whether the courier needs to wait for your response before leaving."
        }
      ],
