          "text": "In Milan, checking the route is part of preparing an order. Area B covers much of the city and restricts more polluting vehicles; Area C regulates central access, generally with a charge for eligible vehicles unless exempt. These are distinct rules and also matter for goods transport. Pedestrian streets, driveways and reserved lanes may prevent stopping at the address. Agree on a lawful handover point rather than asking a courier to ignore restrictions. Check current municipal rules for the intended day and vehicle."
